    "a": "The explicit label is visible: a mark on the image, an opening-frame notice on video, an audio cue. The implicit label is metadata written into the file header, carrying content attribute information, the producing service name or code, and a content ID. Article 4 requires the explicit label to be present in a downloaded or exported file."
  },
  {
    "q": "Does the label have to survive download?",
    "a": "The explicit one, yes. Article 4 requires a service offering download, copy or export to ensure the file contains a conforming explicit label. The implicit metadata label is not what that clause is about, which is a distinction a lot of secondary commentary loses."
  },
