    "q": "Can a studio deliver an unlabeled master?",
    "a": "Article 9 contemplates it. A provider may hand over content without the explicit label where the user applies for it and the user agreement sets out the user's labeling obligation and liability, and the provider keeps the related logs for at least six months. So the unlabeled master is conditional on paperwork and record keeping, not simply available on request."
  },
  {
    "q": "Where in a production pipeline does the label usually get lost?",
    "a": "At export, on the evidence of the regulator's own November 2025 enforcement round, which found labels omitted when files were exported and metadata identifying the producer missing. Retouch and batch resizing are the other common points, because both write a new file and few tools carry custom header metadata across."
  },
  {
    "q": "What are the penalties?",
    "a": "There is no schedule of penalties in the Measures themselves. Enforcement is routed back through authorities and instruments that already existed, and what has been published so far reads as account handling and content clearance rather than financial penalties. If someone quotes you a number, ask which instrument it comes from, because it is not coming from this one."
  }
];
